   "text": "The first three files, in order, are:\n\n1. `exllamav3/__init__.py`\n2. `exllamav3/architecture/__init__.py`\n3. `exllamav3/architecture/afmoe.py`\n\nThe first file, `exllamav3/__init__.py`, is the package's top-level entry point. It sets environment defaults before importing PyTorch\u2014disabling the ROCm profiler registration thread by default and configuring Triton's AMD backend on ROCm builds\u2014then imports `torch` with a helpful error message if it's missing. It also applies default CUDA allocator settings (expandable segments) unless the user has configured them or is on Windows/ROCm, and finally re-exports the library's main public API: `Config`, `Model`, `Tokenizer`, `MMEmbedding`, cache classes, generator/job classes, filters, and sampler symbols."
