   "finish": "stop",
   "text_sha256": "951f81725a98777f521b8241f1bc9a671c26d65ae2629dc103f1bcf2a18efe09",
   "text": "The first three files, in order, are:\n\n1. `exllamav3/__init__.py`\n2. `exllamav3/architecture/__init__.py`\n3. `exllamav3/architecture/afmoe.py`\n\nThe very first file, `exllamav3/__init__.py`, is the package's top-level entry point. It sets environment defaults before importing torch (disabling the ROCm profiler registration thread and pointing Triton at the AMD backend on ROCm builds), raises a clear error if PyTorch is missing, and configures the CUDA caching allocator to use expandable segments unless the user has already set `PYTORCH_CUDA_ALLOC_CONF` or is on Windows/ROCm. It then re-exports the library's public API \u2014 `Config`, `Model`, `Tokenizer`, `MMEmbedding`, the cache classes, and the generator/job/filter classes \u2014 so users can import them directly from `exllamav3`."
  },
