   "text_sha256": "141484a396b2a96f15aadd07b36917de288de3a2528c447bf61d6e87bab1c512",
   "text": "The first three files, in order, are:\n\n1. `exllamav3/__init__.py`\n2. `exllamav3/architecture/__init__.py`\n3. `exllamav3/architecture/afmoe.py`\n\nThe first file, `exllamav3/__init__.py`, is the package entry point. It sets environment defaults before importing torch (disabling the ROCm profiler registration thread and pointing Triton at the AMD backend on ROCm builds), raises a clear error if PyTorch is missing, and configures the CUDA caching allocator with expandable segments unless the user already set `PYTORCH_CUDA_ALLOC_CONF` (skipped on Windows, ROCm, or when `EXL3_EXPANDABLE_SEGMENTS=0`). It then re-exports the library's public API \u2014 `Config`, `Model`, `Tokenizer`, `MMEmbedding`, the cache classes, `Generator`/`Job`/`AsyncGenerator`/`AsyncJob`, the filters, and the sampler namespace \u2014 so users can import everything from the top-level package."
